  <!-- PERMIT -->
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="permit-title">
    <div class="container--narrow">
      <span class="eyebrow">Rotterdam municipality</span>
      <h2 class="section-title" id="permit-title">Permit process for facade signage</h2>
      <p class="section-subtitle">Most facade signage in Rotterdam requires an Omgevingsvergunning. The municipality checks dimensions, illumination, location and aesthetic fit.</p>
      <div class="prose">
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Permit-free:</strong> vinyl lettering up to 0.5 m&sup2; total area, no illumination, not in a protected streetscape or on a listed building.</li>
          <li><strong>Permit required:</strong> signage exceeding 0.5 m&sup2;, all illuminated signs (light boxes, channel letters, neon), dimensional letters above certain dimensions.</li>
          <li><strong>Aesthetic review:</strong> standard part of the permit application. Assesses whether the sign fits the streetscape and building appearance.</li>
          <li><strong>Heritage and protected streetscapes:</strong> separate review by heritage authority. Stricter rules: no illuminated boxes, restricted dimensions, understated designs.</li>
          <li><strong>Lead time:</strong> six to twelve weeks for standard permit, twelve to sixteen weeks for heritage listed buildings.</li>
          <li><strong>Permit fees:</strong> typically 250 to 500 euro depending on project scope.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:var(--space-5) var(--space-6);background:var(--surface-mute);border-left:4px solid var(--brand);border-radius:var(--radius-md);margin:var(--space-6) 0;">
        <div style="font-size:var(--text-xs);font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-muted);margin-bottom:var(--space-2);">Permit tip</div>
        <p style="font-size:var(--text-base);color:var(--ink);line-height:var(--lh-base);">Rotterdam municipality requires an Omgevingsvergunning for facade signage exceeding 0.5 m&sup2;, illuminated signs and signage in protected streetscapes. Lead time six to twelve weeks. We prepare the full application including technical drawings and aesthetic review submission. For heritage buildings we coordinate with the heritage authority.</p>
