  <!-- FAQ ACCORDION -->
  <section class="section section-soft" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
    <div class="container--narrow">
      <div class="section-header">
        <span class="eyebrow">Frequently asked questions</span>
        <h2 class="section-title" id="faq-title">FAQ: Facade Signage Rotterdam</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="faq" role="list">
        <div class="faq__item" role="listitem">
          <button class="faq__question" aria-expanded="false">What does facade signage cost in Rotterdam?</button>
          <div class="faq__answer"><p>Five transparent packages. Vinyl text from &euro;295. 3D dimensional letters from &euro;795. Illuminated light box from &euro;1,495. Channel letters from &euro;2,495. Complete facade package from &euro;3,995. All prices include VAT, design, materials and installation. Permit fees billed separately at cost.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq__item" role="listitem">
          <button class="faq__question" aria-expanded="false">Do I need a permit for facade signage in Rotterdam?</button>
          <div class="faq__answer"><p>Usually yes. Rotterdam municipality requires an Omgevingsvergunning for facade signage exceeding 0.5 m&sup2;, illuminated signs and signage on heritage buildings. Small vinyl lettering under 0.5 m&sup2; is typically permit-free. We advise upfront and prepare the full application. Lead time six to twelve weeks.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq__item" role="listitem">
          <button class="faq__question" aria-expanded="false">What types of facade signage are there?</button>
          <div class="faq__answer"><p>Four main types: vinyl lettering (self-adhesive film on facade or glazing), 3D dimensional letters (CNC-milled PVC or Dibond, stand-off mounted), light box (rectangular LED-backlit box), and channel letters (individually lit LED letters in their own housing). Channel letters give the most premium effect.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq__item" role="listitem">
          <button class="faq__question" aria-expanded="false">How long does facade signage last?</button>
          <div class="faq__answer"><p>Vinyl lettering five to seven years. PVC dimensional letters fifteen to twenty years; Dibond up to twenty-five years. Light boxes and channel letters ten to fifteen years; LED modules may need replacement after five to seven years.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq__item" role="listitem">
          <button class="faq__question" aria-expanded="false">What is the difference between a light box and channel letters?</button>
          <div class="faq__answer"><p>A light box is a rectangular enclosure where the full name or logo is displayed inside one uniformly lit unit. Lower cost and faster to install. Channel letters are individual letters, each with its own LED strip and housing. Each letter lights independently &mdash; premium architectural look. Channel letters suit retailers, restaurants and offices wanting a high-end appearance.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq__item" role="listitem">
          <button class="faq__question" aria-expanded="false">Can you repair existing facade signage?</button>
          <div class="faq__answer"><p>Yes. We replace failed LED modules in light boxes and channel letters, reattach loose dimensional letters and restore partially damaged vinyl lettering. We first inspect to assess the damage and also work on signage not originally installed by us.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq__item" role="listitem">
          <button class="faq__question" aria-expanded="false">How long does a facade signage project take?</button>
          <div class="faq__answer"><p>Vinyl lettering one to two weeks. 3D dimensional letters three to four weeks. Light box four to six weeks. Channel letters six to eight weeks. If a permit is required, add six to twelve weeks for the permit process.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq__item" role="listitem">
          <button class="faq__question" aria-expanded="false">Does the facade need preparation before installation?</button>
          <div class="faq__answer"><p>For vinyl lettering the facade must be clean and dry; we clean the surface ourselves. For dimensional letters and light boxes we use chemical anchors or expansion fixings depending on facade type. For channel letters, electrical preparation is needed; we coordinate this with your electrician or arrange it ourselves.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq__item" role="listitem">
          <button class="faq__question" aria-expanded="false">What materials do you use for dimensional letters?</button>
          <div class="faq__answer"><p>PVC for letters up to 30 cm high: lighter, more economical, fifteen to twenty year lifespan. Dibond (aluminium composite) for larger letters and high facades: premium finish, up to twenty-five years. For heritage or listed buildings: bronze or gilt letters produced via certified foundries.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq__item" role="listitem">
          <button class="faq__question" aria-expanded="false">Do you work across the Rotterdam region?</button>
          <div class="faq__answer"><p>Yes. Rotterdam, Schiedam, Vlaardingen, Capelle aan den IJssel, Barendrecht, Spijkenisse, Ridderkerk, Krimpen aan den IJssel and Maassluis. No travel charges for installation within these locations.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq__item" role="listitem">
          <button class="faq__question" aria-expanded="false">Can you install signage on heritage listed buildings?</button>
          <div class="faq__answer"><p>Yes, in coordination with the municipality and heritage authority. Listed buildings have stricter rules: no illuminated boxes, restricted dimensions, understated designs. We typically use bronze or gilt dimensional letters. Experience with permit applications in Rotterdam centre, Kralingen and Delfshaven.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq__item" role="listitem">
          <button class="faq__question" aria-expanded="false">What warranty do you give on facade signage?</button>
          <div class="faq__answer"><p>Two years on material defects, installation and colour stability for vinyl and dimensional letters. For LED modules in light boxes and channel letters a five-year manufacturer warranty applies; failures within this period are replaced free of charge.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

